<title>USA: AEP cuts Cook, Mich. nuclear unit output.</title>
<headline>AEP cuts Cook, Mich. nuclear unit output.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Electric Power Co's Indiana/Michigan Power Co cut production at its 1,090 megawatt (MW) Cook nuclear unit 2 for maintenance on a main feedwater pump, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission said Monday.</p>
<p>The NRC, in its daily plant status report, said the unit was running at 55 percent of capacity this weekend, down from 100 percent Friday.</p>
<p>The adjacent 1,020 MW Cook unit 1 was operating at 96 percent output, NRC said.</p>
<p>The Cook nuclear power station is in Bridgman, Mich.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1622))</p>
